Mode	                process.roles
=====                 =============
Combined node	        broker,controller
Broker-only node	    broker
Controller-only node	controller

1. Combined Mode (Development)
process.roles=broker,controller

Used for: local development, testing, small setups

One JVM acts as: Kafka broker AND KRaft controller

2. Broker-Only Node
process.roles=broker

This node handles: topic data, producers, consumers,partitions
BUT it does NOT manage cluster metadata.
We must connect it to external controllers.

3. Controller-Only Node
process.roles=controller

This node manages: metadata, leader election, cluster coordination
It does NOT store topic data.

Production Best Practice
========================

For production KRaft clusters:

3 dedicated controllers
+
multiple broker nodes

Why Separate Controllers?
=========================

Advantages:
better scalability
better metadata performance
improved stability
controller isolation
safer failover

Confluent Platform 8.x Recommendation
=====================================

Environment	Recommended
>> Local/dev	: broker,controller
>> Production	: Separate controllers + brokers

1. Controller 1 Config(controller1.properties)
==============================================

process.roles=controller

node.id=1

controller.quorum.bootstrap.servers=localhost:9093,localhost:9094

listeners=CONTROLLER://:9093

controller.listener.names=CONTROLLER

listener.security.protocol.map=CONTROLLER:PLAINTEXT

log.dirs=/tmp/kraft-controller-1-logs


